legacy/docs/spec/references.md:270:| `tests/programs/error_2i_ref2_unused_alias_fn_type_returns_ref.con` | `reject:E0236:REF-2@1` | `ref2g16` | `-` |
legacy/docs/spec/references.md:680:<a id="REF-6"></a>
legacy/docs/spec/references.md:681:### REF-6. Reference bindings are never introduced by `let` and never assigned
legacy/docs/spec/references.md:683:**REF-6@2.** No `let` binds a reference, no reference binding (a parameter, a borrow-block binder or an arm-scoped pattern binder) is ever the target of an assignment, no constant initializer borrows (a cast to a reference type counting as a borrow), and no generic instantiated inside an `assert`, an `assume` or a ghost initializer is instantiated at a type that could hold a reference under substitution.
